# Logs
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local

# Generated by graphify
graphify-out/
.claude/skills/

# Editor directories and files
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?
*.tsbuildinfo

# Local-only notes and build guides
CLAUDE.md
IOS_BUILD.md
ANDROID_BUILD.md

# Environment / secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Vault data. The app exports encrypted backups and imports CSVs that hold
# passwords in plain text (Settings warns about this) -- neither belongs in
# a repo, least of all this one.
*.enc
*.csv
vault-backup*

# Android signing material. Leaking a keystore is unrecoverable: it is the
# only thing that can ever sign an update to a published app.
*.jks
*.keystore
*.p12
*.pepk
key.properties
keystore.properties
local.properties

# Android / Gradle build output. The generated project under
# src-tauri/gen/android ignores its own; these catch anything outside it.
.gradle/
.cxx/
*.apk
*.aab
*.aar

# iOS. src-tauri/gen/apple itself is meant to be committed -- these are the
# per-user and secret parts of it.
xcuserdata/
*.xcuserstate
DerivedData/
*.mobileprovision
*.p8
*.cer
*.certSigningRequest
